ool with a  blow bow and a plastic membrane that  lets swimmers talk to each other  up to 15 feet away he fits the idea to  toys r us  and they ordered the products from him  keep those wrists warm  playing in the snow is fun but let's  face it it's super  cold there are gloves to keep your hands  warm but up until catherine gregory  there was nothing out there to keep your  wrists warm  in 1994 catherine was 10 years old and  super tired of playing in the snow with  cold wrists  so she invented wristies wristies are  fuzzy sleeves that people can wear  underneath their coats and gloves she  tested the wristies out on her girl  scout troupe before going on qvc  she then became the youngest person to  sell a product on qvc  isn't that crazy all because she  couldn't stand having cold wrists  cool treat popsicles are pretty much a  staple at every pool or  summer event but that wasn't always the  case can you imagine a time before  popsicles  in 1905 the temperature in san francisco  had reached an all-time low  frank epperson had mixed soda water  powder and water in a glass and  accidentally  left a stirring stick in the mixture  when he went to bed after it sat out in  the cold all night it froze over  so frank had unknowingly invented the  first popsicle at just 11 years old  initially frank didn't do anything with  his invention but in 1922  he ended up giving out the treat at a  fireman's ball and  everyone loved it crayon sleeves  coloring with crayons can be fun from  time to time but the problem is every  time we go to use crayons it seems like  half of the pack is broken  cassidy goldstein was experiencing this  too and was super annoyed by it  so when she was 11 she started looking  through her arts and craft supplies  until she found  a plastic tube that was initially  intended to keep roses fresh when they  were shipped she put the crayon into the  tube and made her first version of  crayon holders  in 2006 she was named youth inventor of  the year  by intellectual property owners  education foundation  the money that cassidy earns from her  invention helped cover most of the  college expenses  and even helped her to get an apartment  in new york city when she graduated  magnetic paper putting up wallpaper is  usually a seriously long  seriously boring process but in 2006  sarah buckle decided that she wanted to  be able to decorate her school locker  without having to go through the process  of putting on wallpaper she also hated  the idea of having to take the wallpaper  down at the end of the year  when she finished eighth grade her  father became the ceo  at magnacard so sarah gave her dad her  idea and asked him to make magnetic  wallpaper  her dad loved the idea and they got to  work now the magnetic wallpaper is sold  at target  rite aid and staples man candles a lot  of people think that candles are for  girls with scents named after flowers  and sunny days  so in 2010 13 year old hartmane was  making fun of the candles that his  sister was giving out for her school  fundraiser he then got the idea to make  more manly sense  so he used the money he made from his  newspaper route and thus  man can candles were born the candles  came in scents like coffee  new mint and fresh cut grass just two  years after inventing the candles  hart had so much business that he had to  rent a warehouse and employ  five people babysaver lately in the news  there have been a lot of reports of  parents leaving their babies in the car  sometimes the parent is busy and forgets  the baby is even in there  unfortunately in the summer babies  cannot survive sitting in hot cars for  long periods of time  so andrew pelham invented a device to  stop this from happening  it's called easy baby saver and it's  made of rubber bands and duct tape it  stretches across the driver's side door  and reminds parents that their kids are  in the car  any time they try to open the door he  entered the invention into the rubber  band contest  for young inventors and won second place  smart will  distracted drivers aren't good for  anyone to combat this  a team of teenagers came up with an  amazing device  together tj everts jayden evarts and  brayton everetts invented the smart  wheel device which clips onto the wheel  of a car  the device uses sensing technology to  let drivers know when they are  distracted  it also has an app that can track  drivers driving habits and let them know  when their driving has improved isn't  that the coolest thing  we bet it will save a lot of lives can  you imagine a world without distracted  drivers that's definitely a future that  we would love to live in  that's it for 10 genius kid inventions  that will blow you away  were you shocked by some of these  inventions let us know in the comments  see you next time

